abilities of selecting a pear from Q in each case, weighted by the probability of that case occurring:\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum from P) = P(Pear from Q | Apple moved) * P(Apple moved | Not Plum) + P(Pear from Q | Pear moved) * P(Pear moved | Not Plum)\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum from P) = (3/11) * (3/7) + (4/11) * (4/7)\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum from P) = 9/77 + 16/77\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum from P) = (9 + 16) / 77\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum from P) = 25/77\n\nTo express this as a decimal rounded to 2 decimal places:\n25 \\ 77 `is approximately` 0.324675...\nRounding to two decimal places gives 0.32.\n", "answer": 0.32}
