not a plum, is the sum of the probabilities of selecting a pear in each case, weighted by the probability of that case occurring:\\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum moved) = P(Pear from Q | Apple moved) * P(Apple moved | Not Plum moved) + P(Pear from Q | Pear moved) * P(Pear moved | Not Plum moved)\\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum moved) = (3/11) * (3/7) + (4/11) * (4/7)\\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum moved) = 9/77 + 16/77\\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum moved) = (9 + 16) / 77\\nP(Pear from Q | Not Plum moved) = 25/77\\n\nTo convert this fraction to a decimal rounded to two decimal places:\\n25 \\ 77 `is approximately` 0.324675...\\nRounding to two decimal places gives 0.32.\\n", "answer": 0.32}
