{"solution": "Let W be the total work required to complete the mosaic mural. The work rate of an artisan is the fraction of the work completed per day.\n\nMr. Thompson's work rate = 1/28 of the mural per day.\nMs. Rodriguez's work rate = 1/42 of the mural per day.\nMr. Chen's work rate = 1/84 of the mural per day.\n\nFor the first 7 days, all three artisans worked together. Their combined work rate is the sum of their individual rates:\nCombined rate (first 7 days) = (1/28) + (1/42) + (1/84)\nTo sum these fractions, find a common denominator, which is the least common multiple of 28, 42, and 84. LCM(28, 42, 84) = 84.\nCombined rate (first 7 days) = (3/84) + (2/84) + (1/84) = (3 + 2 + 1)/84 = 6/84 = 1/14 of the mural per day.\n\nThe amount of work done in the first 7 days is:\nWork done in 7 days = Combined rate * Time = (1/14) * 7 = 7/14 = 1/2 of the mural.\n\nThe remaining work is:\nRemaining work = Total work - Work done = 1 - 1/2 = 1/2 of the mural.\n\nAfter 7 days, Mr. Chen leaves the project. Mr. Thompson and Ms. Rodriguez continue working together. Their combined work rate is:\nCombined rate (after 7 days) = (1/28) + (1/42)\nUsing the common denominator 84:\nCombined rate (after 7 days) = (3/84) + (2/84) = 5/84 of the mural per day.\n\nThe time taken to complete the remaining 1/2 of the mural by Mr. Thompson and Ms. Rodriguez is:\nTime for remaining work = Remaining work / Combined rate (after 7 days) = (1/2) / (5/84)\nTime for remaining work = (1/2) * (84/5) = 84/10 = 8.4 days.\n\nThe total number of days from the beginning to complete the mural is the sum of the time spent with all three artisans and the time spent with only two:\nTotal time = Time in first period + Time in second period\nTotal time = 7 days + 8.4 days = 15.4 days.\n\nRounding the answer to two decimal places, we get 15.40 days.", "answer": 15.40}
